# Do not delete this file, and do not add `vendor` or `build` to it.
#
# `npm run package:zip` (wp-scripts plugin-zip) builds its file list with
# npm-packlist, which applies ignore sources in this order:
#
#   builtins -> package.json "files" -> .npmignore -> .gitignore
#
# Later sources win, so .gitignore outranks the "files" allowlist. Because
# .gitignore contains /vendor/ and /build/ -- both required at runtime -- the
# "files" list alone would silently ship a plugin that fatals on activation.
# npm-packlist disables .gitignore entirely whenever .npmignore has rules, so
# the mere existence of this file (with real rules) is what makes packaging
# correct. See AGENTS.md > Packaging & release.
#
# Entries below also outrank "files", so only list things that must never ship.

AGENTS.md
Gruntfile.js
bin
alphalisting.zip
changelog.md
composer.lock
css/*.scss
node_modules
.vscode
.wordpress-org

# scripts/ is webpack SOURCE, bundled into build/index.js -- except two files
# that PHP reads at runtime, so it cannot be excluded wholesale here (these
# rules outrank the "files" allowlist):
#   scripts/blocks/attributes.json      <- src/GutenBlock.php reads this
#   scripts/alphalisting-widget-admin.js <- functions/enqueues.php enqueues this
scripts/blocks/*.js
scripts/components
